.TH RATT-LANGUAGE-SERVER 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ratt-language-server \- provide static Rattscript editor services over LSP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ratt-language-server
.RB [ \--stdio ]
.br
.B ratt-language-server
.RB { \--help " | " \-h " | " \--version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ratt-language-server
serves the Language Server Protocol using JSON-RPC messages on standard input
and standard output. An editor normally starts it as a child process and
exchanges Content-Length-framed messages. The default transport is standard
I/O; \--stdio explicitly selects the same transport. There is no TCP listener.
.PP
Services include static diagnostics, completion, hover information, go-to
definition, and document symbols for Rattscript. The server analyzes documents
without executing build actions or evaluating script top-level statements.
It handles document changes and imports to provide editor feedback.
.PP
Configure your editor's language-server command as ratt-language-server
\--stdio. Rattpack ships editor add-ons under share/rattpack/addons in the
installation prefix. Keep standard output dedicated to protocol messages;
diagnostics from the server itself go to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--stdio
Use standard input/output for LSP traffic. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display usage and exit. Supply this option alone.
.TP
.B \--version
Display the version and exit. Supply this option alone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates help/version output, or a protocol exit following shutdown.
1 indicates a server failure or termination without the shutdown handshake.
2 indicates unsupported arguments. An editor should send shutdown, wait for
its response, then send exit for an orderly termination.
.SH EXAMPLES
Editor command and arguments:
.PP
.nf
ratt-language-server \--stdio
.fi
.PP
Inspect usage without starting a session:
.PP
.nf
ratt-language-server \--help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rattsc (1),
.BR rattbuild (1),
.BR rattspec (1)
.PP
See the editor add-ons and development chapters of the installed Rattpack
manual.
